            "review_title": "Review at Banh tom Ho Tay",
            "review_text": "Khoa Pelczar\n12 contributions\n0\nVery bad attitude\nApr 2024 • Couples\nTo be honest, if I didn't crave shrimp cakes, I definitely wouldn't go there. Attitude from parking to staff and management. Besides the shrimp cakes, the jellyfish salad I ordered was not delicious. I don't know what you're going to eat here, but you'll have to pay for parking and an additional VND 10,000 service fee. We collect service fees from guests but also collect parking fees. Not to mention the manager said: \"It's the same in the south, where we don't charge a car fee.\"\nSorry, I don't need to know if it's north or south because I don't care about the region, everyone is Vietnamese, but the attitude coming from this manager is so wrong. Large restaurants, once customers have come to eat and serve food at the restaurant, will never charge additional parking fees or service fees. I will try to find another restaurant that has this shrimp cake to support, but I will never return to this restaurant.\nShrimp cake: 5*\nService: 3*\nManager: 1*\nParking lot: 1*\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nShow original\nWritten April 15, 2024",
